The MIT License above covers this repository, with one exception.

Ten files that implement the Shared Brain backend are licensed under the
Curator Enterprise License v1.0 instead. They are listed explicitly, by path,
in LICENSES/ENTERPRISE-FILES.txt, and the license text is in
LICENSES/LICENSE-ENTERPRISE.txt.

If a file's exact path is not in LICENSES/ENTERPRISE-FILES.txt, it is MIT.

The Curator Enterprise License is free for personal, educational, academic,
evaluation, development, testing, and research use. It also permits production
use of the free, GitHub-backed Shared Brain at no charge, permanently,
including by organizations -- "GitHub-backed" meaning public github.com, which
is the only GitHub the shipped adapter can talk to. Because Curator Enterprise
license keys do not yet exist, it also permits all other organizational
production use of THIS release at no charge, permanently. Each release's
enterprise-licensed files convert to the MIT License two years after that
release is published. Nothing is restricted retroactively.

See README.md ("Licensing") for a plain-English summary.
